### Irregular Terrain Model (Longley-Rice) — parts of libradio

Radio propagation over terrain — the reason VOR, NDB and DME signal strength
depends on what sits between you and the station.

- **License:** [CDDL-1.0](https://opensource.org/license/cddl-1-0) — SPDX
  `CDDL-1.0` — covering **the parts of libradio we ship** (see below), not the
  underlying ITM code
- **Attribution:** the thread-safety modification present in these files is
  **Saso Kiselkov's** contribution to libradio
- **Obtained from:** [libradio](https://github.com/skiselkov/libradio) by Saso
  Kiselkov, vendored byte-identical and unmodified
- **Underlying algorithm:** created by the U.S. Department of Commerce
  **NTIA/ITS**, Institute for Telecommunication Sciences

The two files we ship carry an NTIA banner and **no copyright notice or license
block of any kind**. That is deliberate upstream: libradio has no
repository-level license and headers Kiselkov's own sources file by file —
`itm_c.cc` and `navrad.c` each open with a CDDL block and an explicit copyright
line — and those headers are pointedly absent from the ITM files. We do not ship
either of the CDDL-headered files.

What we *do* redistribute of his is the **thread-safety refactor** inside the ITM
sources, which replaced the original's function-`static` cross-call state with a
single state struct. That contribution is his, and CDDL-1.0 is the license under
which libradio distributes his work — which is why CDDL-1.0 is listed here, and
why its full text ships with the WASM source.

**CDDL-1.0 is not asserted over the NTIA/ITS code itself, and this project
asserts no license of its own over any of it.** The banner names NTIA/ITS as
author of the FORTRAN reference, not of this C++ translation, whose authorship is
unstated upstream — so no claim is made about the translation's status either.

Our own glue is separate and not derived from those files: the bridge wrapper is
an independent reimplementation of the shim libradio ships as CDDL-headered code,
and the surface-constants table was reimplemented from ITU-R P.527 rather than
copied.

### puff — DEFLATE inflate

Decompresses the terrain tiles, so the WASM module needs no zlib at runtime.

- **License:** [zlib](https://opensource.org/license/zlib) — SPDX `Zlib`
- **Copyright:** © 2002–2013 Mark Adler, all rights reserved (version 2.3, 21 Jan 2013)
- **Upstream:** [zlib](https://github.com/madler/zlib), `contrib/puff`

Clause 2 of the license requires that altered versions be plainly marked, so:
**this copy is altered.** The `<setjmp.h>` dependency was removed — the MSFS wasm
sysroot ships no `setjmp.h` — and the original `setjmp`/`longjmp` "out of input"
escape was replaced with an overrun flag and an error return. The inflate
algorithm and its output are unchanged, and the changes are marked in the source.

Clause 1 invites, without requiring, an acknowledgment:
*this product includes software written by Mark Adler.*

